From 0f2785ed64df2087b39bf2c36cd447dda719aea3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 12:41:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] armchina-npu: drop IRQF_ONESHOT from request_irq (no
 threaded handler)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

IRQF_ONESHOT is valid only for request_threaded_irq() with a real
threaded handler. The driver's request_irq() call wraps to
request_threaded_irq(irq, handler, NULL, flags, name, dev) with
thread_fn=NULL, so IRQF_ONESHOT trips a WARN at kernel/irq/manage.c:1502
during __setup_irq.

Driver does NOT use a threaded IRQ — it uses a workqueue
(INIT_WORK + create_singlethread_workqueue), so IRQF_ONESHOT is
inappropriate. Driver's own comment at aipu_irq.c:67-69 calls this out:
'Flag IRQF_ONESHOT is used when sharing interrupts with other devices
using thread_irq. Remove it if you have no such a usage scenario.'
This commit follows that guidance.

Validated: WARN disappears from probe; behavior unchanged (IRQ still
shared via IRQF_SHARED, still uses workqueue bottom half).

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 driver/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/driver/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c b/driver/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c
index a4bad6e..10e912b 100755
--- a/driver/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c
+++ b/driver/armchina-npu/aipu_irq.c
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@ struct aipu_irq_object *aipu_create_irq_object(struct device *dev, u32 irqnum, v
 	 * Remove it if you have no such a usage scenario.
 	 */
 	ret = request_irq(irqnum, aipu_irq_handler_upper_half,
-			  IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_PROBE_SHARED,
+			  IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_PROBE_SHARED,
 			  description, irq_obj->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "request_irq failed: irqnum %u, ret %d", irqnum, ret);
